# Stele environment.
#
# Every variable below is optional. With none of them set the decision console
# still runs end to end: WEEX calls return shaped mock fills and the model chain
# falls through to the local claude CLI, then to the offline stub. Nothing in
# the UI is a dead end without keys.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data source (lib/store/index.ts, the only module that reads this key)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# "fake" reads the seed ledger in lib/data/seed.json, which is what the deployed
# demo and the recording run on. "real" reads closed fills from WEEX and
# attributes them to the thesis that opened them. Anything other than the exact
# string "real" is treated as "fake", and "real" without WEEX credentials falls
# back to the seed as well, so an unset or misspelled value never breaks a
# deploy.
ADAPTER_MODE=fake

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Round store (lib/store/round.ts, the only module that uses these)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both are OPTIONAL. Set them and the round snapshot (theses, positions, logs,
# decisions, the idempotency keys already spent) survives a page reload and a
# cold serverless instance. Leave them unset and the same snapshot lives in a
# module scope singleton, which still walks every step of DEMO.md and only
# loses state when the process restarts.
#
# Any Upstash compatible Redis REST endpoint works. On Vercel, add the Upstash
# integration and it fills both in for you; on Upstash directly, copy them from
# the database page under "REST API". Server only, no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
# There is no migration step and no SQL: the store holds one JSON blob and
# seeds itself on the first read.
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

# Where npm run demo:reset posts. Only scripts/demo-reset.mjs reads it.
# Defaults to http://localhost:3000.
STELE_BASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WEEX OpenAPI v3
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Create the keys at weex.com under API Management, then have the AI Wars II
# organizers add your UID and your server's static IP to the allowlist. Until
# that approval lands, uploadAiLog rejects the write and Stele queues it locally.
# Read by lib/weex.ts.
WEEX_API_KEY=
WEEX_API_SECRET=
WEEX_API_PASSPHRASE=

# API host. Leave as is unless WEEX gives you a regional endpoint.
WEEX_API_HOST=https://api-contract.weex.com

# "sim" routes orders through the demo futures endpoints (/capi/v3/sim/...),
# "live" sends real orders with real money. Default is sim. Flip to live only
# after the 11 step API checklist in HANDOFF.md passes on sim.
WEEX_VENUE=sim

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model chain (lib/agent.ts)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Get a key at console.anthropic.com. This is the submission path: the recorded
# demo must run with this set, because the AI model token allocation is awarded
# on proof of real model usage.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional model override. Defaults to claude-opus-5.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# No key? Install the claude CLI (npm i -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code) and
# lib/agent.ts uses it automatically for local development. No variable needed.
